B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The crate\u2019s tests were run on a Linux sandbox for this page. All six ring tests pass there, using the non-Windows fallback (a plain thread_local! with a Drop impl). The Windows FLS code in this file is not exercised by them; it is covered by the hook crate\u2019s stress and self-load harnesses on a real Windows build."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("limits"))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"10.5 MiB per allocating thread","the cost of the flat ring; a program that spawns thousands of short-lived threads allocates and frees that much for each."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"drops are silent","dropped is counted and never reported."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"start-at-zero draining","the fairness question above."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"the registry is a Mutex","acceptable off the hot path, but the first allocation on each thread does take it."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"FlsFree trade-off","after shutdown(), live threads\u2019 rings are never marked dead, by design."))
