B.a.h(n,A.a(q,'The test walks a full life in four ticks and checks nodes().len() at each step: 2 after both are born, 1 after the parent is freed (the diff still reports the parent in remove and the child in update), 2 again when a sentinel allocation advances the clock and sweep flips the child to Orphan, and 1 after the child is freed. The header comment explains why it checks every tick rather than the end: "a test that only checked the final count could pass even if eviction happened too early and silently corrupted a tick\u2019s diff". In tick 3 it also reproduces the main.rs Tick step by calling mark_updated on each changed id. It confirms that orphan detection does not need the dead parent\u2019s struct. Notice that the sentinel\u2019s timestamp, 6,000,010, is written as the "owner_free_ts + tau + margin", while sweep actually compares against the child\u2019s own alloc ts (1). Both are past tau, so the test passes either way. The comment describes a rule slightly different from the one the code applies.'))
