B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"crates/heaplens-daemon/tests/hook_owner_free_no_crash.rs \xb7 lines 146-157",'fn target_debug_dir() -> std::path::PathBuf {\n    let test_exe = std::env::current_exe().unwrap();\n    test_exe\n        .parent()\n        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n        .expect("cannot determine target dir from test exe path")\n        .to_path_buf()\n}\n\nfn target_path(name: &str) -> std::path::PathBuf {\n    target_debug_dir().join("examples").join(format!("{name}.exe"))\n}'))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"target_path finds the example in target/<profile>/examples/ and the injector at target/<profile>/heaplens-injector.exe, both relative to the test\u2019s own location. The assertions that they exist carry the build command, which here says cargo build --release (while the tests will also work with a debug profile if the pieces are built the same way; the profile directory is whichever one the test itself is in)."))
