B.a.h(n,A.b("a flaw I noticed"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The size check at lines 295-299 compares every alloc event for an expected pointer against the expected size. The sibling test, hook_self_load_spawned_thread.rs, found that this is unsound and fixed it in commit 084ddf9: the harness\u2019s own println! calls make heap allocations that the hook faithfully captures, and an address can be used by one of those incidental allocations (size 30, say) before the harness\u2019s scripted allocation (size 32) gets it. Comparing the first, or here every, event for that pointer then reports a false mismatch. The fix, comparing the last alloc event per pointer, lives in that file\u2019s find_alloc_size_mismatches and was not applied here. So this test may carry the same latent flake as the one that was fixed; I have not seen it fail."))
