B.a.h(n,A.b("why this file exists"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The UI refresh redesigned the app as a ribbon across the top, a rail down the side, and panels in between. Seven small pieces recur in those places, and they were pulled into one file so that the look of the app is decided in one place. Everything here is presentation: no providers, no knowledge of nodes or the daemon. It reads colors and type from XynorashTheme and nothing else."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("toggles sized to the text beside them"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 5-12","/// A toggle sized to actually match the height of the label text it sits\n/// next to, rather than the stock Material [Switch]'s fixed proportions.\n/// Scaling a real `Switch` down (`Transform.scale`) still left it visibly\n/// taller than a 12px label, because Material's switch track has its own\n/// fixed minimum size that a naive scale factor doesn't reliably land on\n/// \u2014 this widget's dimensions are set directly instead, so \"match the\n/// text\" is exact rather than approximated.\nclass CompactSwitch extends StatelessWidget {"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The first two widgets exist because, per the doc comment, the stock widgets did not match the label height. A Material Switch scaled down with Transform.scale was still visibly taller than a twelve pixel label, because the switch track has its own minimum size and a scale factor does not land on it. So CompactSwitch is built from primitives with its size set directly: track width is twice the height, the thumb is the height minus four, and a 150 millisecond animation moves it. The idea is stated as exact rather than approximated."))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 27-57","  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final width = height * 2;\n    final thumbSize = height - 4;\n    return GestureDetector(\n      behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque,\n      onTap: () => onChanged(!value),\n      child: AnimatedContainer(\n        duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 150),\n        width: width,\n        height: height,\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(2),\n        decoration: BoxDecoration(\n          color: value ? XynorashTheme.cyan.withValues(alpha: 0.55) : Colors.white24,\n          borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(height / 2),\n        ),\n        child: AnimatedAlign(\n          duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 150),\n          curve: Curves.easeOut,\n          alignment: value ? Alignment.centerRight : Alignment.centerLeft,\n          child: Container(\n            width: thumbSize,\n            height: thumbSize,\n            decoration: BoxDecoration(\n              color: value ? XynorashTheme.cyan : Colors.white70,\n              shape: BoxShape.circle,\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"CompactSegmented applies the same fix to the view-mode toggle: a pill whose height is a parameter, an option list generic over the value type, a cyan tint on the selected option. The ribbon instantiates it as CompactSegmented of ViewMode. The generic type means it is not tied to the view enum, but it is only used once. One gap: both widgets are a GestureDetector over a container, with no Semantics and no focus handling, so they cannot be reached by keyboard or announced by a screen reader through anything in this file. A later version could add that."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("the signature device"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 130-136","/// The app's one signature visual device: a thin sci-fi-HUD corner\n/// bracket at each corner of [child], instead of a Material rounded-card\n/// border. Applied consistently to every major panel (ribbon, right\n/// rail, insights panel, node detail) \u2014 restrained (thin stroke, low\n/// alpha by default) rather than decorative, the way a real cockpit\n/// display's panel edges are functional framing, not ornament.\nclass HudFrame extends StatelessWidget {"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 163-191","class _HudCornerPainter extends CustomPainter {\n  _HudCornerPainter({required this.color, required this.cornerLength, required this.strokeWidth});\n\n  final Color color;\n  final double cornerLength;\n  final double strokeWidth;\n\n  @override\n  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {\n    final paint = Paint()\n      ..color = color\n      ..strokeWidth = strokeWidth\n      ..style = PaintingStyle.stroke\n      ..strokeCap = StrokeCap.round;\n    final len = cornerLength.clamp(0.0, size.shortestSide / 2);\n\n    // Top-left\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(0, len), Offset.zero, paint);\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset.zero, Offset(len, 0), paint);\n    // Top-right\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(size.width - len, 0), Offset(size.width, 0), paint);\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(size.width, 0), Offset(size.width, len), paint);\n    // Bottom-left\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(0, size.height - len), Offset(0, size.height), paint);\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(0, size.height), Offset(len, size.height), paint);\n    // Bottom-right\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(size.width - len, size.height), Offset(size.width, size.height), paint);\n    canvas.drawLine(Offset(size.width, size.height), Offset(size.width, size.height - len), paint);\n  }"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"HudFrame is the one visual idea in the app, and the comment calls it restrained: a thin corner bracket at each corner instead of a rounded card border. Eight line segments, two per corner, at 12 pixels long and 1.4 wide by default, in the cyan hairline color at low alpha. The comment\u2019s argument is functional: a cockpit display\u2019s panel edges are framing, not ornament."))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"Details in the painter. The corner length is clamped to half the shortest side, so a very small panel does not draw brackets that cross over. It paints in the foreground painter, above the child, so the brackets stay visible on top of panel fills. shouldRepaint compares all three fields. It is used by the right rail and the insights panel."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("ribbon pieces"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 200-203",'/// One grouped, visually-separated unit in the top bar (e.g. "attach\n/// control", "summary metrics"). A thin vertical divider marks the\n/// boundary between cells so related controls read as one group without\n/// needing a heavier border around every cell.'))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 238-243","/// A plain-language label paired with its technical value \u2014 the dual-level\n/// legibility pattern used throughout the top bar and right rail: the\n/// label is always the human-readable name of the thing, the value is\n/// always the real, precise data next to it. An optional [tooltip] gives\n/// the plain-sentence definition on hover; the label/value themselves are\n/// never replaced by the tooltip, only supplemented."))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"TopBarCell is one grouped unit in the ribbon, with an optional vertical divider after it in the purple at 35 percent alpha. The padding is 22 by 14, and the comment says it grew from 12 by 6 when the ribbon began to span the full window, because cells packed to the left looked unfinished. MetricTile is the label-and-value pair the ribbon uses for its counters: the label is normal text in the plain language name, the value is bold monospace, so it reads as data. An optional tooltip supplies a one-sentence definition without replacing either part. The comment calls this dual-level legibility, and it is the principle of the whole app: the label tells you what, the value tells you exactly."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("empty means something"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 275-281",'/// An explicit empty/waiting state \u2014 used anywhere a panel would otherwise\n/// render blank (no target attached, no node selected, daemon not yet\n/// connected). Always says what\'s missing and, where relevant, what to do\n/// about it, per the legibility rule that empty panels are never bare.\n/// Styled as a terminal prompt line (`> message`) rather than a plain\n/// italic sentence \u2014 an empty panel in this app reads as "awaiting input",\n/// which a prompt communicates more precisely than a caption would.'))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"EmptyState is the rule that no panel is ever bare. It always says what is missing and, when relevant, what to do about it. It is drawn as a terminal prompt line, > message, in dim monospace, with an optional icon, because an empty panel in this app means awaiting input and a prompt says that more precisely than a caption. The tests rely on the exact text: node_detail_test expects > no node selected."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("the rail section"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"heaplens_flutter/lib/widgets/ui_common.dart \xb7 lines 309-321, 334-369","/// One always-on, non-collapsible section of the right rail \u2014 no chevron,\n/// no tap-to-collapse, always showing [child] in full. [muted] demotes a\n/// section's visual weight (smaller, dimmer text) for developer-diagnostic\n/// content that isn't the primary audience's concern, without hiding it.\n///\n/// Pass [expand]: true (default false) to have this section grow to fill\n/// any remaining vertical space in its parent `Column` \u2014 used for the last\n/// section (verbose logs) so the rail's total content stretches to fill\n/// the window instead of stopping partway down and leaving dead space.\n/// Requires the immediate parent to be a `Column`/`Flex`, per `Expanded`'s\n/// own contract.\nclass RailSection extends StatelessWidget {\n  const RailSection({\n...\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final titleColor = muted ? Colors.white38 : XynorashTheme.cyan;\n    final header = Padding(\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(12, 10, 12, 6),\n      child: Text(\n        XynorashTheme.bracketLabel(title),\n        overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n        style: XynorashTheme.sectionHeader(color: titleColor, fontSize: muted ? 10 : 12),\n      ),\n    );\n    final body = Padding(\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(12, 0, 12, 12),\n      child: child,\n    );\n\n    final content = Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n      mainAxisSize: expand ? MainAxisSize.max : MainAxisSize.min,\n      children: [\n        header,\n        if (expand) Expanded(child: body) else body,\n        if (!expand) const Divider(height: 1, color: Colors.white12),\n      ],\n    );\n\n    if (!expand) return content;\n    return Expanded(\n      child: Column(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n        children: [\n          const Divider(height: 1, color: Colors.white12),\n          Expanded(child: content),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"RailSection is a titled block: the title through bracketLabel and sectionHeader, a body with 12 pixel side padding and a hairline divider below. muted lowers the title to ten point, dim grey, for developer diagnostics. The expand option makes the section an Expanded child with the divider above it, for filling leftover space; the comment explains it needs a Column parent. As noted in the right rail page, nothing uses expand today, so the second half of the build method is dead code kept for a layout that was dropped."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("edge cases"))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"fixed pixel sizes","all dimensions are literals, tuned for the desktop window. No text scaling or density handling."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"HudFrame on tiny areas","the clamp prevents inverted corners; a zero-size child paints nothing meaningful."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"Tooltip needs an Overlay","MetricTile and EmptyState-based tooltips depend on a Material app ancestor, which main.dart provides."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("how it is tested"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"Through its users. control_bar_test.dart taps the keyed orphanOnlySwitch, which is the CompactSwitch, and checks the view-mode toggle writes the provider. node_detail_test.dart finds the EmptyState text. The painter and RailSection have no direct test; a pixel regression in the brackets would pass."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("history"))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"1cfb7f9 (2026-07-19)","feat(flutter): UI refresh. The only commit; it creates the file as the shared vocabulary of the new layout."))
