B.a.h(o,A.b("the whole decision, in thirty lines"))
B.a.h(o,A.d("ini","heaplens_flutter/pubspec.yaml \xb7 lines 1-1, 5-5, 19-22, 30-32, 36-41, 43-45, 52-52, 58-63","name: heaplens_flutter\n...\npublish_to: 'none' # Remove this line if you wish to publish to pub.dev\n...\nversion: 1.0.0+1\n\nenvironment:\n  sdk: ^3.12.1\n...\ndependencies:\n  flutter:\n    sdk: flutter\n...\n  cupertino_icons: ^1.0.8\n\n  flutter_riverpod: ^2.5.0\n  web_socket_channel: ^2.4.0\n  vector_math: ^2.1.4\n  fl_chart: ^0.69.0\n...\ndev_dependencies:\n  flutter_test:\n    sdk: flutter\n...\n  flutter_lints: ^6.0.0\n...\nflutter:\n\n  # The following line ensures that the Material Icons font is\n  # included with your application, so that you can use the icons in\n  # the material Icons class.\n  uses-material-design: true"))
B.a.h(o,A.a(q,"Almost all of the file is boilerplate that flutter create wrote and that I left standing. The lines above are the ones that carry a decision. The scaffold commit message says which: it adds flutter_riverpod, web_socket_channel, vector_math and fl_chart per locked decisions on state management and on hand-written models with no code generation, and it fixes the target at the Dart VM and Windows desktop only."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("what each dependency is for"))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"flutter_riverpod ^2.5.0","all state. Every provider file in lib/providers uses it. The code uses StateProvider for the small toggles (paused, selection, view mode, the three filters) and Notifier/NotifierProvider for anything with behaviour (the graph, the attached target, the target diagnosis). The caret range allows 2.x releases from 2.5.0 up."))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"web_socket_channel ^2.4.0","the daemon connection. It is imported in exactly one file, lib/providers/ws_provider.dart, which keeps socket concerns out of the widgets."))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"vector_math ^2.1.4","positions and velocities in the force layout. Imported by lib/simulation/force_layout.dart and by lib/widgets/graph_canvas.dart, and by the force layout test."))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"fl_chart ^0.69.0","the size-over-time sparkline in node_detail.dart, its only importer. A single small line chart is the whole use of a charting library."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("the dependency that nothing uses"))
B.a.h(o,A.a(q,"cupertino_icons is in the list because flutter create put it there. A search of lib/ and test/ finds no reference to it, so it looks like a leftover dependency. Removing it would be a one-line change. It is the one line in the manifest that reads as scaffold default rather than decision."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("what is missing, on purpose"))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"assets and fonts","the flutter section has only uses-material-design: true; the assets and fonts blocks are still the commented generator examples. The theme file says why for fonts: no custom font is bundled, because a system font used consistently reads more intentional than an inconsistently applied downloaded one. Consolas is the monospace family and the code falls back to Cascadia Code and then the generic monospace."))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"publishing","publish_to: none is set, which is the right setting for an application that is not a pub.dev package."))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"description","still reads A new Flutter project. It is metadata that shows up nowhere a user would look, and it shares its fate with the README."))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"version","1.0.0+1, the generator default; the app has no release process in this directory that would bump it."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("the platform choice, and what it does to the manifest"))
B.a.h(o,A.a(q,"Because the target is only the Dart VM on Windows, the manifest has no web configuration, no platform conditionals, and no JS-compatible alternatives. The reason is in the scaffold commit message: the daemon sends pointers and timestamps as 64-bit values in JSON numbers, and the commit cites the protocol crate\u2019s documented seam note as the reason web is out. Choosing the Dart VM means an int is a real 64-bit integer, so the models can use plain int fields and the app never needs a big-integer package. That is why the dependency list has no bignum or JSON-codegen entry: the platform decision removed the need for them."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("the SDK constraint"))
B.a.h(o,A.a(q,"environment: sdk: ^3.12.1 lets the code use current Dart syntax without caveats. You can see it in the source: switch statements with pattern cases such as case DetachResultResponse(ok: true) and case TargetExitedResponse(:final pid) in target_provider.dart, record typedefs such as the sparkline sample typedef in node_detail.dart, and wildcard parameters written as (_, _) in the diagnostics provider test. None of those would compile on an older SDK, so the constraint is a real floor, not a default."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("how it is tested"))
B.a.h(o,A.a(q,"A manifest has no unit test of its own. flutter_test comes from the SDK, and flutter_lints is wired up by analysis_options.yaml, which includes the flutter ruleset. The check that matters is that flutter pub get resolves, and pubspec.lock records the result of that resolution, committed next to this file."))
B.a.h(o,A.b("history"))
B.a.h(o,A.c(q,"56d5e41 (2026-07-06)","the scaffold commit. The message names the four additions and the platform decision. Nothing has touched the file since, which means the whole of the app, through the UI refresh of 2026-07-19, fit inside these four dependencies."))
