B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"Keys are buffer-local, and set in an LspAttach callback that waits 120 milliseconds, because LSP configurations may set keys such as <C-k> again on every attach, and these must come after them. The map helper does not override an existing buffer-local map with a different description, except for the insert-mode key, which is forced: the macro popup first, and the server\u2019s signature help as the fallback."))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"lua/xyno_macros/tools.lua \xb7 lines 2449-2455,2464-2472",'  local group = vim.api.nvim_create_augroup("xyno_macros", { clear = true })\n  vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd("FileType", {\n    group = group,\n    pattern = "rust",\n    callback = function(ev)\n      schedule_hints(ev.buf)\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ "TextChanged", "InsertLeave", "BufWritePost" }, {\n...\n  vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd("InsertCharPre", {\n    group = group,\n    callback = function(ev)\n      if vim.bo[ev.buf].filetype ~= "rust" or not ra_client(ev.buf) then\n        return\n      end\n      local ch = vim.v.char\n      if ch == "(" or ch == "[" or ch == "{" or ch == "!" then\n        vim.schedule(function()\n'))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"setup stores the keymap table, registers the commands, and creates one augroup. FileType rust schedules a hint scan and adds the buffer-local autocmds that rescan after changes. InsertCharPre calls the popup when the typed character is an opening bracket or a bang. TextChangedI refreshes an open popup. InsertLeave and BufLeave close it. The last loop catches buffers that were already open when setup ran. One small thing to know: the FileType callback adds new buffer-local autocmds to the shared group every time it fires, so a buffer whose filetype event fires twice can carry duplicates; the code does not guard against it."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("design decisions"))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"Three-valued matching","complete, viable, impossible. A call being typed is never complete, so a boolean matcher would show nothing."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"Budgets everywhere","the matcher steps, the scan size, the retry counts and the cargo-expand timeout are all bounded."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"Server first, fallbacks after","rust-analyzer for definitions and expansions, tables for std macros, cargo expand for what the server cannot expand."))
B.a.h(n,A.c(q,"Refuse rather than guess","the TOML editor, the module path of cargo expand and the macro-path checks all decline when unsure."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("tested by"))
