B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"A card is a Container with a raised surface, a 10-pixel radius and a one-pixel border, 14 pixels apart from the next. Compare it to the bibliography tab: lines 50 to 57 of bibliography_tab.dart are the same decoration, down to the numbers. The two files each build the card by hand. There is a shared SidebarCard in the repo, but for the sidebar, and nothing equivalent for the output side. With two users the duplication is cheap; a third tab with the same card would be the moment to extract it."))
n.push(B.b)
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The inside is a Row with crossAxisAlignment start. The number sits at the left and the text column takes the rest, aligned to the top, so a long description grows downward without pulling the number to the middle."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("the number badge"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"lib/widgets/output/tabs/outline_tab.dart \xb7 lines 31-47","                Container(\n                  width: 36,\n                  height: 36,\n                  alignment: Alignment.center,\n                  decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                    color: colors.teal.withValues(alpha: 0.12),\n                    shape: BoxShape.circle,\n                  ),\n                  child: Text(\n                    part.partNumber,\n                    style: AppTypography.serif(\n                      weight: FontWeight.w700,\n                      color: colors.teal,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n                const SizedBox(width: 14),"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"A 36 by 36 circle in a 12-percent teal tint with the numeral in bold serif, teal on teal. The size is fixed, which works for I, II and III. The widest of those is III, and a longer string (a model that answered \u201cPart three\u201d) would overflow the circle, because nothing here shrinks the text. The prompt makes that unlikely, but it is the one place where the layout trusts the model."))
B.a.h(n,A.b("the text column"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"lib/widgets/output/tabs/outline_tab.dart \xb7 lines 48-63","                Expanded(\n                  child: Column(\n                    crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                    children: [\n                      Text(\n                        part.title,\n                        style: AppTypography.serif(\n                          fontSize: 17,\n                          color: colors.ink,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      const SizedBox(height: 6),\n                      MarkdownText(part.description),\n                    ],\n                  ),\n                ),"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The title is in the serif face at 17 pixels, one point larger than a bibliography title, since a part heading is a heading and a book title is a line of a list. The description goes through MarkdownText, which lists outline descriptions explicitly among the prose fields it renders. The Expanded gives the column the remaining width, so long text wraps. Without it the Row would ask the Text for an unbounded width and Flutter would report an overflow."))
