B.a.h(n,A.b("why this file exists"))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The lead of the guide describes its audience: someone who wants to add a dependency, pick its features or start a workspace without leaving the editor. It is separate from the README, which is written for people already in the repository. This guide is one of six, each about one job: diagnostics, debugging, tests and coverage, cargo workspaces, a git safety net and the Island Dark theme. Each is a separate page with its own address, title, description and share card, and each documents what the configuration really does. The spec enforces that last part: every command and key the guides name must exist in the running configuration."))
n.push(B.b)
B.a.h(n,A.b("the head carries the metadata"))
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"site/guides/neovim-cargo-workspaces/index.html \xb7 lines 1-13",'<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n<meta charset="utf-8">\n<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">\n<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src \'self\'; img-src \'self\' data:; media-src \'self\'; style-src \'self\'; script-src \'self\'; base-uri \'none\'; form-action \'none\'">\n<title>Cargo workspaces, features and crates in Neovim | xynovim</title>\n<meta name="description" content="Create Rust binaries, libraries and workspaces, add crates with their features and fix missing derive features from Neovim: :CrateAdd, :CrateFeatures and more.">\n<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light">\n<meta name="theme-color" content="#1e1f22" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">\n<meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f7f9" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">\n<link rel="canonical" href="https://xynorash.github.io/xynovim/guides/neovim-cargo-workspaces/">\n<link rel="icon" href="../../assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">\n'))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The page is a complete document with a language and a viewport. The first policy is the Content Security Policy as a meta tag: default-src self, images from self and data, media from self, styles and scripts only from self, no base element and no form action. The policy lists only self as a source, which backs the footer\u2019s statement that the site makes no external requests. The title is the headline plus the site name, under the 60 characters the spec allows; the description is the sentence that appears under it in search results, between 120 and 160 characters by the spec. The meta tags for colour scheme and theme colour are given once for dark and once for light, matching the stylesheet\u2019s two palettes."))
n.push(B.b)
B.a.h(n,A.d(o,"site/guides/neovim-cargo-workspaces/index.html \xb7 lines 12-28",'<link rel="canonical" href="https://xynorash.github.io/xynovim/guides/neovim-cargo-workspaces/">\n<link rel="icon" href="../../assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">\n<meta property="og:type" content="article">\n<meta property="og:site_name" content="xynovim">\n<meta property="og:locale" content="en">\n<meta property="og:title" content="Cargo workspaces, features and crates in Neovim | xynovim">\n<meta property="og:description" content="Create Rust binaries, libraries and workspaces, add crates with their features and fix missing derive features from Neovim: :CrateAdd, :CrateFeatures and more.">\n<meta property="og:url" content="https://xynorash.github.io/xynovim/guides/neovim-cargo-workspaces/">\n<meta property="og:image" content="https://xynorash.github.io/xynovim/assets/og/neovim-cargo-workspaces.png">\n<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">\n<meta property="og:image:height" content="630">\n<meta property="og:image:alt" content="xynovim guide: Cargo workspaces, features and crates in Neovim, a new workspace tree with a member crate">\n<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">\n<meta name="twitter:title" content="Cargo workspaces, features and crates in Neovim | xynovim">\n<meta name="twitter:description" content="Create Rust binaries, libraries and workspaces, add crates with their features and fix missing derive features from Neovim: :CrateAdd, :CrateFeatures and more.">\n<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://xynorash.github.io/xynovim/assets/og/neovim-cargo-workspaces.png">\n<meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="xynovim guide: Cargo workspaces, features and crates in Neovim, a new workspace tree with a member crate">\n'))
B.a.h(n,A.a(q,"The canonical link names the clean URL with a trailing slash, and the Open Graph and Twitter blocks repeat title and description, give an absolute image URL (the generated card for this guide, 1200 by 630) and alt text for it. The spec requires absolute URLs on the canonical host, a card under 300 KB and alt text. They are the tags a link preview is built from."))
